  "stimulus": {
    "driver_ohm": 10000.0,
    "vdd_v": 1.0,
    "edge_s": 1e-12,
    "t_stop_s": 4e-11,
    "delay": "50% of the victim source to 50% of the victim hub",
    "energy": "integral of v*i at the victim source, 0 to t_stop"
  },
  "idealisations": [
    "each line is driven by an ideal step through a 10 kohm resistor and measured at its lumped RC hub (the deck's own topology: pin - R - hub - C)",
    "only the victim's two nearest same-level neighbours switch; every other line is held at 0 V by an ideal source (a stiff quiet line)",
    "reference network: R from klt mom's PEEC resistance; hub-to-ground C = klt mom ground + adjacent-level + non-nearest same-level coupling; the nearest-neighbour couplings are explicit hub-to-hub capacitors; each neighbour copies the victim's R and ground C (symmetry ASSUMED) and neighbour-to-neighbour coupling is dropped",
    "deck network: the netlist `klt extract --deck asap7 --parasitics` wrote, verbatim; it has no same-level coupling, but every hub's C returns to the floating `vsubs` node (1e12 ohm to ground), which couples the lines weakly, so quiet and opposite differ slightly even there",
    "critical-net path: refused by every FinFET deck (phase 1), reported 'unsupported', never zero-filled",
    "quasi-static lumped RC, no inductance, no device nonlinearity; the energy is the integral of v*i at the victim's source over 0-40 ps"
  ],
